      "question": "Draw $\\triangle ABC$, with $AB = 6$ cm, $BC = 7$ cm and $CA = 7$ cm. Draw the circumcircle of $\\triangle ABC$. Let the circumcentre be $O$. Measure $OA$, $OB$, $OC$.",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**Draw the triangle:** Draw $AB = 6$ cm. With $A$ as centre draw an arc of radius $7$ cm, and with $B$ as centre draw an arc of radius $7$ cm. The arcs meet at $C$. Join $AC$ and $BC$."
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**Draw the circumcircle:** Draw the perpendicular bisectors of $AB$ and $BC$. Their intersection is the circumcentre $O$. With $O$ as centre and radius $OA$, draw the circle."
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**Measure the distances:** Since $O$ is the circumcentre, $OA = OB = OC = R$, the circumradius. For this triangle, $R \\approx 3.87$ cm."
        },
        {
          "step": 4,
          "content": "**Verify with the formula:** $R = \\frac{abc}{4\\Delta}$. Here $a = 7$, $b = 7$, $c = 6$. The height to base $AB$ is $h = \\sqrt{7^2 - 3^2} = \\sqrt{40} = 2\\sqrt{10}$, so $\\Delta = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 2\\sqrt{10} = 6\\sqrt{10}$. $$R = \\frac{7 \\times 7 \\times 6}{4 \\times 6\\sqrt{10}} = \\frac{294}{24\\sqrt{10}} = \\frac{49}{4\\sqrt{10}} \\approx 3.87 \\text{ cm}$$"
        }
      ],
