      "questionNumber": 4,
      "question": "What is the least possible radius of a circle through two points $A$ and $B$?",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**Recall:** The centre of any circle through $A$ and $B$ lies on the perpendicular bisector of $AB$."
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**Minimise the radius:** The radius is the distance from the centre to $A$ (or $B$). This distance is smallest when the centre is the midpoint of $AB$."
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**Conclusion:** The smallest circle has $AB$ as its diameter, so its radius is $\\frac{AB}{2}$."
        }
      ],
